    Container(work_artifacts, "Work Artifacts", "Markdown", "Runtime outputs: board, backlog, plans, reports")

    Rel(skills, agents, "Spawns via Agent()")
    Rel(hooks, skills, "Triggers on Claude events")
    Rel(eval_system, skills, "Tests skill behavior")
    Rel(agents, docs, "Produces documentation")
    Rel(skills, work_artifacts, "Manages sprint artifacts")
```

## Bounded Context Map

| Context | Ownership | Ubiquitous Language |
|---------|-----------|-------------------|
| Skill Management | skills/ | skill, frontmatter, invocation, trigger phrase |
| Agent Execution | agents/ | sub-agent, brief, permission mode, gate |
| Hook Automation | hooks/ | event, matcher, command hook, prompt hook |
| Evaluation | evals/ | assertion, benchmark, iteration, baseline |
| Sprint Planning | .work/ | roadmap, backlog, board, sprint, feature |
| Documentation | agent_docs/ | SRS, HLD, LLD, IMP, TST, feature |

## Service Decomposition

| Service | Responsibility | Data Ownership |
|---------|---------------|----------------|
| Skill Orchestrator | Workflow control and agent spawning | Skill definitions, pipeline state |
| Agent Executor | Phase-specific artifact generation | Agent configurations, templates |
| Hook Engine | Event-driven automation | Hook scripts, event matchers |
| Eval Engine | Empirical testing and benchmarking | Evaluation configs, results, metrics |
| Sprint Manager | Roadmap/backlog/board management | Sprint artifacts, status tracking |
| Doc Generator | Phase documentation output | Architecture docs, feature specs, tech design |

## Communication Patterns

| Integration | Pattern | Protocol |
|-------------|---------|----------|
| Skill → Agent | Request/Response | Agent() tool call |
| Hook → Claude | Event Publication | Claude Code event system |
| Claude → Plugin | Plugin Loading | File system, YAML/JSON |
| Eval → Skill | Test Execution | File-based I/O |
| Sprint → Docs | Document Sync | File-based Markdown |

## Security Architecture

- **Auth Model**: No built-in authentication. Relies on Claude Code's session-based access control.
- **Trust Boundaries**: Plugin executes within Claude Code process boundary. No network calls.
- **Data Protection**: All data stored locally in `.work/` and `agent_docs/`. No at-rest encryption needed.

## Infrastructure Architecture

Single-process deployment within Claude Code CLI. No container orchestration, no cloud services. Plugin is loaded from local filesystem. Git worktrees provide isolation for concurrent development tasks.
